    </aside>

    <!-- the narrative -->
    <div class="jx-steps">

      <article class="jx-step" data-stage="1" data-zone="open" data-time="9:52">
        <div class="jx-when"><i class="ti ti-clock"></i> 9:52 AM &middot; Before the doors open</div>
        <h2>The associate signs in. Nothing to type.</h2>
        <p>Rotating QR-code sign-in at the register with nothing to type, plus optional facial recognition. One code per associate, every sign-in logged. Check a price, see active promotions, or read current stock counts before anyone signs into the terminal.</p>
        <ul class="jx-list">
          <li>QR associate login, or face, or a password where you want one</li>
          <li>Pre-login price check</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="jx-more" href="/features/access-identity/">See Access &amp; Identity <i class="ti ti-arrow-right"></i></a>
      </article>

      <article class="jx-step" data-stage="2" data-zone="open" data-time="9:58">
        <div class="jx-when"><i class="ti ti-clock"></i> 9:58 AM &middot; The drawer, the sync, the day</div>
        <h2>Cash is consistent before the first sale.</h2>
        <p>Drawer memos, blind counts, variance alerts, and safe checklists. Pre-flight routines keep cash consistent at open and close. Drawer memos linked to a single device, or several registers tracking one shared cash drawer simultaneously.</p>
        <ul class="jx-list">
          <li>Flexible drawer architecture</li>
          <li>The app and its data are on the device, so a network outage does not stop the register</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="jx-step" data-stage="3" data-zone="floor" data-time="10:41">
        <div class="jx-when"><i class="ti ti-clock"></i> 10:41 AM &middot; She walks in</div>
        <h2>The register is in the associate's hand, not at the back.</h2>
        <p>Full-featured POS on iPhone or iPad. Sell from the fitting room, stockroom, or floor, untethered from the cash wrap. The same point of sale on iPad at the counter and iPhone in an associate's hand, working from one cart, one customer and one inventory count.</p>
        <ul class="jx-list">
          <li>Mobile-first POS, native to iOS</li>
          <li>Training to be on register: under 5 minutes</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="jx-step" data-stage="4" data-zone="floor" data-time="10:44">
        <div class="jx-when"><i class="ti ti-clock"></i> 10:44 AM &middot; "Something warm for the weekend"</div>
        <h2>The most knowledgeable coworker on your floor.</h2>
        <p>An AI assistant built into the associate's handheld. It has read every product tag, knows every care label, and never tires of "do we have this in a different color?" Associates ask it the way they would ask a colleague and get an answer, with pictures, in seconds.</p>
        <ul class="jx-list">
          <li>Ask in plain language: "Something warm for a weekend in the mountains" brings back the products that fit</li>
          <li>Answers with pictures, so the customer sees them too</li>
          <li>Save and share: keep products for later and share them with the customer</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="jx-more" href="/features/product-data/">Explore product data <i class="ti ti-arrow-right"></i></a>
      </article>

      <article class="jx-step" data-stage="5" data-zone="fitting" data-time="10:52">
        <div class="jx-when"><i class="ti ti-clock"></i> 10:52 AM &middot; Fitting room, wrong size on the rack</div>
        <h2>Out of stock? Ship from another store in 3 taps.</h2>
        <p>Item-level visibility in stores, warehouses and channels. Receiving, transfers, and RFID cycle counts, from the mobile POS, in minutes. Highlights from 39+ omnichannel workflows: BOPIS, ship-from-store, and BORIS. Any location can fulfill, with routing rules you set.</p>
        <ul class="jx-list">
          <li>Scan a tag: pull up the product information for the item in hand</li>
          <li>Endless aisle and save the sale</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="jx-more" href="/platform/oms/">See order management <i class="ti ti-arrow-right"></i></a>
      </article>

      <article class="jx-step" data-stage="6" data-zone="fitting" data-time="10:58">
        <div class="jx-when"><i class="ti ti-clock"></i> 10:58 AM &middot; She has been here before</div>
        <h2>One profile per customer, not one per store.</h2>
        <p>Purchase history, preferences, wishlists, notes and loyalty status on the associate's screen at the register. The same customer record in each market, so a shopper is recognized wherever they buy. New customers scan a QR code to enroll in loyalty themselves, no manual entry, no errors, and a real lift in sign-ups.</p>
        <a class="jx-more" href="/features/customer-data/">See customer data <i class="ti ti-arrow-right"></i></a>
      </article>

      <article class="jx-step" data-stage="7" data-zone="pay" data-time="11:05">
        <div class="jx-when"><i class="ti ti-clock"></i> 11:05 AM &middot; Rung up right there</div>
        <h2>The line at the register is six deep. She never joins it.</h2>
        <p>An associate walks to the fitting room with an iPhone and rings the shopper up right there. Every line in the transaction can be adjusted on its own: split associate attribution, custom text notes, gift messaging, and tax exemptions per line. Manual percentage or dollar-off discounts, coupon overrides, and direct price overrides for online price-matching, all logged and permission-controlled.</p>
        <ul class="jx-list">
          <li>Promotions calculate inside the cart with no associate intervention: spend-more-get-more thresholds and multi-item BOGO applied automatically</li>
          <li>Stackable coupons, generic or customer-specific such as birthday rewards, set to stack or stand alone</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="jx-step" data-stage="8" data-zone="pay" data-time="11:08">
        <div class="jx-when"><i class="ti ti-clock"></i> 11:08 AM &middot; She pays on the associate's iPhone</div>
        <h2>Tap to Pay on iPhone. No separate card reader.</h2>
        <p>Native NFC on the iPhone processes contactless cards directly on the device, no separate card reader hardware. Integrated merchant platforms including Adyen and Razorpay, plus cash, credit memos, foreign-currency cash conversion, and digital installment programs. Unlimited split payments across methods: store credit and cash together on one ticket, in any combination.</p>
        <ul class="jx-list">
          <li>Dynamic checkout QR codes on screen for regional mobile wallets, such as Aplazo in Mexico</li>
          <li>Card data is encrypted at capture and never stored on the POS</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="jx-step" data-stage="9" data-zone="pay" data-time="11:09">
        <div class="jx-when"><i class="ti ti-clock"></i> 11:09 AM &middot; The receipt, and the screen facing her</div>
        <h2>Print, email, or preview. Split one ticket into gift receipts.</h2>
        <p>Segmented receipts: print, email, or preview, and split one large ticket into multiple gift receipts assigned item by item. At the counter, a second screen at every register, run by the same POS app, targets each customer by profile and purchase history, and switches to checkout when the queue needs it. Customers join loyalty by scanning a QR code.</p>
        <ul class="jx-list">
          <li>Vendors pay to reach customers at the moment of purchase</li>
          <li>Shopper display included with every deployment</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="jx-step" data-stage="10" data-zone="back" data-time="2:15">
        <div class="jx-when"><i class="ti ti-clock"></i> 2:15 PM &middot; Stockroom, mid-afternoon count</div>
        <h2>End-to-end RFID built into the POS, with no middleware.</h2>
        <p>The RFID logic is native to the POS and runs on the reader hardware you choose, for 99.9% inventory accuracy and one-tap checkout. Receiving, live counts and tag printing, all from the mobile POS. Every unit tracked by EPC from receiving through to the sale, so sold and unsold are distinguishable at any point.</p>
        <ul class="jx-list">
          <li>Native RFID tracks stock item by item, at 99.9% accuracy</li>
          <li>Self-checkout: drop items in a bin, every tag reads at once, and the cart builds itself</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="jx-more" href="/platform/rfid/">See RFID in action <i class="ti ti-arrow-right"></i></a>
      </article>

      <article class="jx-step" data-stage="11" data-zone="back" data-time="4:30">
        <div class="jx-when"><i class="ti ti-clock"></i> 4:30 PM &middot; An online order, filled from this store</div>
        <h2>Cross-channel returns and exchanges with no sync lag.</h2>
        <p>Return an online order in-store; that inventory is instantly resellable. The system knows when someone is returning one piece of a bundle: it detects single-item returns from a multi-product promotion, and you configure the flow to block the return or warn the associate first.</p>
        <ul class="jx-list">
          <li>Returns &amp; exchanges, promotion-aware</li>
          <li>Transactions suspended with configurable pause reason codes, then retrieved from any device in the store</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="jx-step" data-stage="12" data-zone="close" data-time="9:04">
        <div class="jx-when"><i class="ti ti-clock"></i> 9:04 PM &middot; Close</div>
        <h2>A cash drawer that reconciles.</h2>
        <p>Expected totals stay masked from the counting employee, and discrepancies force a secondary management login to sign off on the shortage or overage. Automated reconciliation with standard deposit logs, plus locally required fiscal summaries such as Zeta reports. Native fiscal compliance: VAT, GST, NF525, TSE, handled in the platform rather than by a local vendor, in 40+ countries.</p>
        <ul class="jx-list">
          <li>Blind count &amp; audit controls</li>
          <li>Paid-in / paid-out recorded natively, the mid-day cash pulled for store supplies included</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="jx-more" href="/platform/scalability/">See global operations <i class="ti ti-arrow-right"></i></a>
      </article>

